#====================================================================
# Draft: serialize OHOS native compressed input pipe lifetime
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-CADICAL-2.1.3-OHOS-POPEN-PIPE-LIFETIME
trigger_tool:           popen|pclose|gzip|make test|cadical
phase:                  upstream-test
error_signature:        parcompwrite.*failed|popen.*failed|gzip.*failed|compressed input.*failed

severity:               2
category:               ohos-popen-pipe-lifetime
match_keywords:         cadical, OHOS, popen, pclose, fread, gzip, compressed input, mutex, pipe race
title:                  Serialize popen to pclose lifetime for native compressed input pipes

root_cause:             On OHOS, concurrently reading compressed command output through native FILE pipes can race across popen creation, stream reads, and pclose teardown. Locking only popen leaves later pipe I/O and teardown unprotected.
affected_scope:         Multi-threaded OHOS native code that reads gzip or other compressed command output with popen, fread, and pclose.
verification_cmd:       make -C test api

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           full-pipe-lifetime-mutex
rec_description:        Guard the complete read-mode popen-to-pclose lifecycle with one recursive mutex. Lock before popen, keep the lock through all reads, and unlock on both successful and failed close paths; do not lock write-mode pipes with the read-pipe mutex.
rec_command:            make -C test api
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      controlled-thread-probe
fallback_description:   If failures remain, run a fixed-thread-count probe that reports popen, read, and pclose failures separately before changing the lock scope.
fallback_command:       ./parcompwrite-probe 100
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       lock only popen|serialize pclose alone|ignore early fread error unlock
forbid_1_reason:        Partial lifetime locking leaves the pipe read and teardown phases unprotected and can preserve the intermittent failure.
forbid_1_consequence:   A small probe can appear less flaky while full upstream tests still fail under thread scheduling and filesystem latency.

principles:             full-lifecycle-locking, platform-independent-posix-guard, evidence-before-lock-scope

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

